|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||
|
| LAB #7 - Problem 2: Fibonacci Sequence
| Group 9
| Cabrera, Niles
| Nellas, Aldrin
| Tibayan, Rafael
|
| Reads N from INPUT and writes the first N terms of the Fibonacci sequence
| (0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, ...) into consecutive words starting at FIBO.
|
| Registers:
|       r0 = terms left to write (starts at N, counts down to 0)
|       r1 = byte offset into FIBO (0, 4, 8, ...; each LONG is 4 bytes)
|       r2 = a = F(i), the term stored this iteration
|       r3 = b = F(i+1), the next term
|       r4 = temp for a + b
|       r5 = flag for N <= 0
|
| Loop invariant (top of iteration i, counting from 0):
|       r2 = F(i), r3 = F(i+1), r1 = 4i, r0 = N - i
|
| Edge cases:
|       N <= 0 writes nothing. The loop tests its counter only after the body
|       runs, so without the guard N = 0 would make r0 = -1 and loop ~2^32
|       times, storing over all of memory.
|       F(47) and later overflow a signed 32-bit word and show as negative,
|       so FIBO reserves 47 words (N <= 47 gives only correct terms).
|
|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||

.include beta.uasm          | include the standard predefined macros

        LD(INPUT, r0)       | r0 = memory[INPUT] = N
        CMOVE(0, r1)        | r1 = 0, offset of FIBO's first word
        CMOVE(0, r2)        | a = F(0) = 0
        CMOVE(1, r3)        | b = F(1) = 1
        CMPLEC(r0, 0, r5)   | r5 = 1 if N <= 0, else 0
        BT(r5, DONE)        | N <= 0: nothing to write, skip the loop

LOOP:   ST(r2, FIBO, r1)    | memory[FIBO + r1] = a
        ADD(r2, r3, r4)     | r4 = a + b
        MOVE(r3, r2)        | a = b
        MOVE(r4, r3)        | b = old a + b
        ADDC(r1, 4, r1)     | offset += 4, next word of FIBO
        SUBC(r0, 1, r0)     | one fewer term left
        BNE(r0, LOOP)       | more terms left: go again

DONE:   HALT()              | stop the simulator

|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||

| Data starts at a fixed address so it is easy to find in the BSim window.
. = 0x19C

| INPUT holds N, the number of terms to generate.
INPUT:
        LONG(7)

| FIBO receives the N terms.
| STORAGE reserves the words. BSim only gives a program enough memory to
| cover its last assembled address (rounded up to a power of two, at least
| 512 bytes). With an empty FIBO label at 0x1A0 memory would end at 0x200,
| so only 24 terms would fit; N = 25 or more would stop with "ST to invalid
| memory location". 47 words holds every term that fits in a signed 32-bit
| word, F(0) through F(46).
FIBO:
        STORAGE(47)
